--- title: Food retail url: https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/tech-insider/food-retail/ hostname: danfoss.com sitename: danfoss.com date: "2011-10-01" fingerprint: bf16dc0b40a054cc --- ### 2026 ## New software release available for the AK-SM 800A series **Version 5.3.x strengthens security, account management, reporting, and StoreView Web functionality** System Manager 800A software package version 5.3.x is now available via the → [Danfoss ADAP-KOOL™ Support site.](https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/downloads/dcs/adap-kool-software/ak-sm-800a/#tab-downloads) **Software release highlights** Release 5.3.x is recommended for all customers and delivers a range of new functionality, usability improvements, cybersecurity enhancements, and software corrections based on customer and market feedback. Highlights include: - Self-service password recovery with authenticator app support o Google Authenticator and 2FAS Authenticator apps have been tested - Enhanced cybersecurity protections and account management features - Improved touchscreen keyboard usability (updated touchscreen keyboard design) - Added support for Schneider EM4200 energy meters - New building pressure monitoring sensor support - New compressor CT-proof alarm functionality - New Temperature Status Report for refrigeration applications (StoreView Web) - Multiple software corrections, reliability improvements, and security updates - Multiple updates to StoreView Web and StoreView Web Desktop o Automatic history collection (StoreView Web Desktop) o History trending functionality o Auto logon (StoreView Web Desktop) o Window controls (StoreView Web Desktop) ## Alsmart Firmware and Alsmart Design new version release **Enhances SM800A integration, USB updates, service-tool responsiveness, and supporting libraries** New Alsmart® firmware, including the Service Tool, and a new Alsmart® Design Tool version are now available for the Alsmart® Universal Controller Platform. The package also includes the current AS-UI04 and expansion firmware for completeness; these firmware components are unchanged in this release. The new Firmware version for all the AS-CX06 and a new correspondent version of Alsmart Design and Service Tool has been released with new functionalities, improvements and features. In addition, Applications Notes are available for download to support and guide on the controllers’ usage and settings. This Software release aims to improve stability, provides new functionalities and interfaces. **Key improvements** - **Improved System Manager SM800A communicatio**n The release includes an important improvement to communication with System Manager SM800A, supporting more reliable integration of Alsmart controllers within existing system architectures. - **Simplified USB update for multiple controllers** The USB update procedure has been improved to simplify commissioning and service activities involving multiple controllers. The same USB device can be used to update multiple Alsmart controllers without manually editing its content between individual controller updates. - **Alsmart Service Tool** This release improves communication performance and responsiveness when working with Alsmart devices, particularly in environments with multiple active sessions. - **IOManager Library Update** Updated the valve configuration to ensure the correct operating parameters. - **LogLibrary Update** Improved the logging functionality to provide more reliable operation under specific timing configurations. **Additional improvements** Alsmart Design 1.10.0012 also improves ASPKG Maker, autogenerated HMI navigation, UserManager API documentation. The release includes additional fixes related to ASPKG Maker display behaviour, CDF database export and ConfigLock download notification. **Application Notes** The latest Application Notes available with this release are: - USB Commands - WebSimulator - Alsmart ASPKG Maker **These documents support the use of key Alsmart®** Universal Controller functionalities. The documents and their change logs can be downloaded from AlsmartCommunity. **Affected products** **Additional information** The Alsmart Firmware, Alsmart Design, Alsmart Service Tool, updated LogLibrary, AS-UI04 firmware, expansion firmware and the three Application Notes can be downloaded here: → [Alsmart Community](https://danfoss.sharepoint.com/sites/AlsmartCommunity/_layouts/15/AccessDenied.aspx?Source=https%3A%2F%2Fdanfoss.sharepoint.com%2Fsites%2FAlsmartCommunity%2FSitePages%2FHome.aspx%3Fovuser%3D097464b8-069c-453e-9254-c17ec707310d%252criccardo.nardetto%2540danfoss.com%26OR%3DTeams-HL%26CT%3D1761914478960%26clickparams%3DeyJBcHBOYW1lIjoiVGVhbXMtRGVza3RvcCIsIkFwcFZlcnNpb24iOiI0OS8yNTEwMDIxMzgxMSIsIkhhc0ZlZGVyYXRlZFVzZXIiOmZhbHNlfQ%253d%253d%26CID%3D63c7d4a1-d0b2-e000-8fb5-1350cca2f723%26cidOR%3DSPO&correlation=4cf048a2-d0de-0001-cc7a-0d9d4107df68&Type=item&name=dc2f24b6-9cfa-4e19-bd04-5a4dd79a71c6&listItemId=1&listItemUniqueId=b7b3d3f0-3c03-4eb3-be57-8e2c979464e0&allowautoredirecttosource=true) Request access to the Alsmart community here: → [registration link](https://alsmart-community-access.danfoss.com/). Stock units will not be recalled or updated. ## AK-PC 782A and AK-PC 782B Web release of new software version 4.30 **Web release expands functionality and corrects minor software issues** Software version 4.30 is now available as a Web release for the AK-PC 782A (PN 080Z0192) and AK-PC 782B (PN 080Z0202) pack controllers. The release supports the continued development of transcritical CO2 packs and corrects minor software issues. **New features (AK-PC 782A and AK-PC 782B)** - Direct HR management o Controlling via Shr4 when using V3sf. o Controlling via Shr8 when using V3hr. o Implementation of Delta-P control via P1/P2 source. o Implementation of S4 alarm trigger. o Implementation of S4 check limit. o Improved S2 check limit. - Integration of new ETS-5T stepper valve (for Vhp, Vrec, GenPI). - Integration of Dry-Ice support from v4.15.07 - Implemented solution for fast start of variable speed compressor, when using VSD safety The current AK-PC 782A and AK-PC782B with software 4.10 or older can be both upgraded to the new SW version 4.30 if desired, by using the Service Tool. The upgrade is optional. The new SW ver. 4.30 is only available as Web release. **Availability** The software version 4.30 is available (since week 38 2026). ## KoolProg version 5.7 maintenance release is available **Enhanced support for EKE, AK-CC, and ERC controllers simplifies firmware updates and reduces programming time** KoolProg version 5.7 is now available for download. This maintenance release introduces auto firmware upgrade support for EKE 100 and EKE 110 controllers, along with updated firmware support for AK-CC25, AK-CC55, EKE 100, and ERC 112D. → [Download the new version here](https://assets.danfoss.com/software/latest/579002/ID502820473954-1001.zip) **Included in 5.7 version** - **Support for updated firmware versions** - **Support for new code numbers for ERC 112D VSC controllers with condenser fan speed control** Added support for new code numbers 080G3428 (red LED) and 080G3429 (blue LED) for PV02 ERC 112D VSC. - **Extended auto firmware upgrade support for EKE-100 and EKE-110 controllers** KoolProg now supports auto firmware upgrades for both EKE-100 and EKE-110 controllers. For EKE-100 controllers running software versions below 3.13, the upgrade is completed through a two-step process: the controller is first upgraded to version 3.13 and then to the latest available software version. For EKE-110 controllers, auto firmware upgrade is supported across all software versions. - **Enable RS-485 communication for AK-CC55 controllers via KoolKey PV** KoolProg now enables direct RS-485 communication via KoolKey for AK-CC55 Single Coil controllers with software version 2.40, Multi Coil controllers with software version 2.01, and Compact controllers with software version 2.32. This feature is supported only with KoolKey PV05 and later versions. **Please note:** KoolKey PV05 is scheduled for release soon and will be communicated through a separate product note. - **Performance enhancement for AK-CC55 and AK-CC25 controller families** Improved programming performance for AK-CC55 and AK-CC25 controller families in KoolProg, reducing programming time from 3–4 minutes to approximately 20–40 seconds. **Please note:** A stable internet connection is required to use this feature. ## PV02 release introduced for ERC 11X STM32 controllers **Component update resolves programming issues and enables customers to return to KoolKey programming** A generic PV02 software release is now available for ERC 112D VSC controllers used in multi-temperature chest cooler and freezer applications. **Description** The programming issue previously reported for ERC 11X STM32 controllers has been resolved by replacing a component within the controllers. Customers who used a gateway as an interim solution to power up the controller can now return to KoolKey programming. **Affected products** **Availability** A new version of ERC 11X STM32 PV02 controllers is now available to order. ## AK-CC25 Pro (BT) software version available **Software update with factory reset and OEM access-code programming support** Software version 1.36 is now available as a web release for AK-CC25 Pro and AK-CC25 Pro BT. The update is not yet pre-installed on controllers released from production; production implementation is planned for the beginning of October 2026. **Key updates** The new software version introduces the following features: **Factory reset functionality:** A Danfoss factory reset can be performed by combining a power cycle with a specific key combination on the display. This restores the controller to the Danfoss factory state, resetting all parameter values, including the network address, access codes, event history, alarm history, and data log history. **OEM access-code programming:** For OEM programming via KoolProg, access codes can be cloned as part of the mass programming process. For the upcoming KoolProg version 5.7.x release, the CDF file must be uploaded manually. The update also resolves minor issues identified in the previous software version. ## Phase-out announced for the WattNode WND energy meter range **Customers should transition to the EM530 energy meter before final orders close on 11/2026** The WattNode WND-WR-MB energy meter **(Code no. 080Z2129)** and related current transformers are being phased out due to low sales demand, supporting ongoing product portfolio optimization and complexity reduction. Customers requiring 3-phase energy monitoring via Modbus RS-485 should transition to the Carlo Gavazzi EM530 energy meter **(Code no. 080Z2130)** which continues as our standard active offering. **Affected products** The following products will be phased out **Timing** The Wattnode energy meter and related CTs is entering its phase-out period due to low market demand, with final orders accepted until November 15, 2026. ## Phase-out for EKC 202x, AK-CC 2xx, and related accessories **New AK-CC25 Pro and Pro BT controllers introduced as the recommended replacements** The release of the AK-CC25 Pro and Pro BT marks the start of the phase-out process for the EKC 202x and AK-CC 2xx controller series and their associated accessories. Customers will be able to place orders for the affected products until December 2026, with the possibility of receiving deliveries through June 2027. We encourage you to prepare your transition to the new AK-CC 25 Pro & Pro BT controllers. **The affected code numbers to be phased out** **All the controllers listed above can be replaced by the new AK-CC25 Pro (BT) with the limitation of support for LON communication.** As LON communication has been declared obsolete by its technology provider, Danfoss will no longer integrate service support for this in our new product. For service replacements (spare parts), a limited number of AK-CC 210 controllers and EKA 179A LON option modules have been secured and will be made available for service replacement only. ## AS-UI04 remote display released for Alsmart® controllers **New panel and wall-mounted interfaces enable remote monitoring and control** Product Version PV01 of the AS-UI04 remote display for the Alsmart® Universal Controller Platform is now released and available for sale. The AS-UI04 can be used in a wide range of applications where remote monitoring and control of Alsmart® controllers is required. Its versatility, user-friendly interface, and customizable display make it suitable for both industrial and commercial environments. **Details** The AS-UI04 provides a user interface for Alsmart® controllers, allowing users to: - Monitor system parameters - Adjust setpoints and other application parameters - View alarms and events - Configure the controller **Affected products** Alsmart User Interface AS-UI04 Panel Mounted (080G6042) and AS-UI04 Wall Mounted Single Pack (080G6044). **Availability** The AS-UI04 panel-mounted and wall-mounted versions are now in stock. **Display characteristics** **Additional information** Data sheets are also available in other languages on the [Alsmart<sup>®</sup> website](https://www.danfoss.com/en/products/dcs/electronic-controls/products/programmable-controllers/alsmart/#tab-overview). Alsmart<sup>®</sup> Design version 1.10.0011 fully supports the new AS-UI04 display and is available now from the dedicated Alsmart® section of the [Danfoss Partner Portal](https://partner.danfoss.com/) or the Danfoss Alsmart<sup>®</sup> Community. For access instructions, see the [Alsmart Partner Portal – Quick setup guide](https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/431645/AM501139320043en-000101.pdf) or use the [Join Alsmart Community](https://alsmart-community-access.danfoss.com/) registration link. For more information, please contact your local sales representative. ## ERC 112D VSC PV02 generic software variant introduced **PV02 release supporting chest cooler and freezer applications** A generic PV02 software release is being introduced for ERC 112D VSC controllers used in multi-temperature chest cooler and freezer applications. **Description** The PV02 release supports generic operating needs, including enhanced condenser fan control, NTC 10K temperature sensor compatibility, and independent sensor calibration for the two operating modes. The relevant product and functional updates are summarized below. **Affected products** **Product Version** PV02 (Generic release) **Key updates** **Availability** Available for ordering with standard lead time. **Customer impact** ERC 112D VSC PV02 provides generic functionality for multi-temperature chest cooler and freezer applications, including configurable condenser fan control, NTC 10K sensor support, and mode-specific temperature calibration. ## AK-CC55 software versions released for Compact, Single Coil and Multi Coil **Expanded controller functionality across injection, defrost, fan control, and configuration** New software versions have now been implemented in production for AK-CC55 Compact (v2.32), Single Coil (v2.40), and Multi Coil (v2.01). All products shipped from Danfoss from week 38 onwards will have the new software pre-installed. The update is indicated by a revised PV number on the product label: PV04 for AK-CC55 Compact and PV05 for AK-CC55 Single Coil and Multi Coil. **Key updates by controller type** **Customer action** Customers using mass programming in production should update existing setting files from the previous software version to the latest version. This can be done in KoolProg by using Set parameters. An updated programming guide is available in the product store. **Required files and tool support** The EPK files required to connect to AK-SM 800A are available in the latest EDF package on the ADAP-KOOL® software site. ## New Alsmart® firmware, Design and Service Tool versions released **Updates add new interfaces, tools, and performance improvements across the Alsmart<sup>®</sup> platform** New Alsmart<sup>®</sup> firmware, Alsmart<sup>®</sup> Design, and Alsmart<sup>®</sup> Service Tool versions are now available for the Alsmart<sup>®</sup> Universal Controller Platform. This release also includes the UI04 firmware. Firmware version 1.44.0004 for all AS-CX06 controllers is released together with corresponding Alsmart<sup>®</sup> Design and Service Tool versions. The updates add new functions, improvements and tools. Several application notes are also available for download to support controller use and configuration. The release improves stability and adds new functions and interfaces. **Key highlights** **Alsmart Firmware version 1.44.0004** Please check the change log included in the package for more details. - CAN-FD Read/Write Support: Enables CAN bus to read/write with dedicated API. - Startup Logo Customization: Custom branding for device startup screens. - UI04 Management: Enhanced HMI support and integration. **Alsmart Design version 1.10.0011** Please check the change log included in the package for more details. - UI04 HMI Simulator: Dedicated simulator with Port Connector enabled by default for CANbus simulation. - Improved SSR Definition Handling: Better Solid State Relay management. - ASPKG Maker: Now available as standalone tool with extended file support. **Alsmart ServiceTool version 2.24.0017** Please check the change log included in the package for more details. - Small improvements and bug fixes - Added “IO configuration” functionality. - Updated to support new controller codes and firmware functionalities with improved debugging, diagnostics, and configuration capabilities. **UI04 Firmware Update (v1.08.0000)** Please check the change log included in the package for more details. - Faster file transfers (2–3 min vs 15 min). - Increased max UI size (2 MB) - Auto-baud rate detection, and no reboot required for baud rate changes. - Mirror Mode: Can mirror Snap-on display for systems without dedicated UI04 software. **Application notes** The application notes provide detailed guidance on using the functions of the Alsmart® Universal Controller. The change log and all available application notes can be downloaded from the Documentation Hub in the Partner Portal. **Affected products** **Alsmart Firmware** v1.44.0004 for Pro/Pro+ and v1.44.0004 for Mid+/Mid/Lite **Alsmart Service Tool** v2.24.0017 **Alsmart Design** v2.24.0017 **UI04 Firmware** v1.08.0000 Stock units will not be recalled or updated. **Downloads** Alsmart Firmware 1.44.0004, Alsmart Design v. 1.10.00011, Service Tool v. 2.24.000517, UI04 1.08.0000 and the Application Notes can be downloaded from the dedicated Alsmart section in the [Danfoss Partner Portal](https://partner.danfoss.com/). Follow the instructions to get access [Alsmart Partner Portal - Quick setup guide](https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/431645/AM501139320043en-000101.pdf) from Alsmart Community ## AK-CC55 software versions released for Compact, Single Coil and Multi Coil **Web releases introduce fixes, restored functions and new control capabilities** New web-release software is available for AK-CC55 Compact (v2.32), Single Coil (v2.40) and Multi Coil (v2.01). The versions resolve issues identified in earlier releases and restore functions across the AK-CC55 portfolio. They are currently only available as web releases through AK-CC Connect or KoolProg and are not pre-installed on controllers from production. A production release is planned for calendar week 35. **New features reintroduced with these new SW versions include:** For OEM and production use, customers must update existing setting files from the previous software version to the latest version using Set parameters in KoolProg. This prepares production lines for the new production software release. ## Selected MCX products scheduled for phase-out Early notice supports service planning, final purchases, and platform migration As part of ongoing product lifecycle management, Danfoss plans to phase out selected MCX products (**not accessories like MMIGRS2 or cables**). This communication is intended to provide timely visibility and transition planning in line with standard discontinuance practice used across the electronics industry. **Affected products and principal reason** **Additional information** For MCX061V and MCX152V, production continuity is impacted by the obsolescence or unavailability of critical components required for manufacturing. For the CRA-related products, the phaseout supports transition toward platforms better suited for long-term cybersecurity maintenance, vulnerability handling, and lifecycle support expectations for connected digital products. **The commercial milestones** MCX08M2 is not part of the immediate phase-out wave. Its phase-out is planned for 2029 to allow time for migration, software porting, validation, and an orderly transition. Customers are encouraged to review current demand, service-spare requirements, and migration planning as early as possible. Where appropriate, successor-platform guidance and transition support will be provided separately. ## AK-SM 800A: Software release 5.1 (incl. StoreView Web update) A new software version 5.1 has been released for the AK-SM 800A System Manager series. The update introduces new features, performance improvements, and system enhancements. It also includes changes to system architecture that affect upgrade and rollback behavior. A new Danux package (4.14.017.194) accompanies this release and should be installed prior to loading the AK SM 800A application update. Both packages are available on the ADAP-KOOL support site. **Software package 5.1 requires Danux 4.14.017.194** **Overview** With the System Manager R5.1.x update, it will no longer be possible to downgrade to an earlier software version as the database structure has undergone significant changes that prevent this. It is strongly recommended to perform a full backup of the system database before starting the update. StoreView Web embedded will remain the default remote user interface, while the previous SvB5 interface will continue to be available for a limited period but will be removed in future releases. **Key updates** Release 5.1.x is a major update for the SM800A Series and is recommended for all customers. It includes multiple enhancements, new features, and fixes. Key highlights are: - Support for Danfoss Drives over Modbus - Increased number of supported Skylight photocells - Ability to set the Alarms screen as the home screen in StoreView Web (SvW) - Additional details added in the System Report - Updates to customer-specific feature (CPT) – not generally available - Fix for issue where Modbus 2 could not be enabled if Modbus TCP was enabled first **Release 5.1 Full Change Log (System Manager)** **Important considerations** For security reasons, the Service Tool (ST 500) port is now disabled by default. To enable a remote Service Tool tunnel connection, the port must be activated via the \[Configuration --> Security\], and it should be disabled again once the tunnel is no longer required. In compliance with cyber security requirements, all new user accounts must be created with strong passwords containing at least 8 characters, including lowercase letters, one uppercase letter, a digit, and a special character.) **Security requirements** To help keep your Danfoss products secure and protected, we strongly recommend implementing cyber security best practices to maximize protection against malicious attacks. **Installation steps** Before proceeding with the update, perform a full unit backup and check for any open alarms. **Step1**: Install Danux 4.14.017.194.lpk - Using StoreView Browser 5 / StoreView Web select OS update and proceed with Danux upgrade - Allow a few minutes to pass with the new OS installed Important notes: This file size package is large and depending on your network speed may take >10 minutes to complete. **Do not interrupt power during the OS update. For systems utilizing DHCP it is advised that this update is performed locally, as IP address change is possible after re-booting.** **Step 2**: Update System Manager firmware (package 5.1.x.spk) - Using StoreView Browser 5 / StoreView Web or local USB Flash drive, select OS update and proceed software upgrade. **Do not interrupt power during the software update** - After installation is complete, review for correct system operation **Approved products** The table below shows approved AK-SM 800A portfolio versions suitable for software 5.1 **Availability** Package 5.1 is released for general update and is available via [ADAP-KOOL® support site](https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/downloads/dcs/adap-kool-software/#tab-overview). Stock units will not be recalled or updated. ## Alsmart® controllers: New AS-CX06 Mid SSR, AS-CX06 Mid+ SSR, and AS-XP10 released New variants have been added to the Alsmart® controller portfolio, including AS-CX06 Mid SSR, AS-CX06 Mid+ SSR, and AS-XP10. These additions extend the platform with updated functionality and increased I/O capabilities. The new models support a broader range of application requirements. **Key features** AS-CX06 Mid (+) SSR: - Certified for CE, UL (Recogn.), RCM, UA, EAC - Programmable with the Alsmart Design 1.10.0008 - Same numbers of I/Os (input and output) as AS-CX06 Pro+/Pro/Mid+/Mid/Lite - The variance is equipped with one SSR in DO 5 position AS-XP10: - Cerfitied for CE and UL (Recogn.) - Expanded I/O capabilities (input and output) compared to AS-XP05(+) (from 17 to 30) **Affected products** - Alsmart Controller AS-CX06 Mid SSR 080G6040 - Alsmart Controller AS-CX06 Mid+ SSR 080G6038 - Alsmart Controller AS-XP10 080G6010 **Availability** The new AS-CX06 Mid SSR, AS-CX06 Mid+ SSR available on stock starting from WK23, AS-XP10 available in stock. The Alsmart Design version 1.10.0008 can be downloaded from Danfoss Partner Portal or from Danfoss Alsmart Community. **Technical specifications** **Additional information** Data sheets are also available in other languages. Download Alsmart Design v. 1.10.0008 from: - A dedicated Alsmart section of the [Danfoss Partner Portal](https://partner.danfoss.com/) - [Danfoss Alsmart Community](https://danfoss.sharepoint.com/sites/AlsmartCommunity/SitePages/Home.aspx). Access guidance - Follow the instructions in [Alsmart Partner Portal - Quick setup guide](https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/431645/AM501139320043en-000101.pdf) and the registration link to request access to the Alsmart Community [Join Alsmart Community.](https://alsmart-community-access.danfoss.com/) ## EKC 202x and AK-CC 2xx controllers: Phase-out initiated The phase-out process for EKC 202x and AK-CC 2xx controllers and related accessories has been initiated. This change follows the introduction of the new AK-CC25 platform. Customers are advised to plan the transition to the replacement products within the defined timeline. **Timeline** Customers will be able to place orders for the affected products **until December 2026**, with the possibility of **receiving deliveries until June 2027**. Please note, however, that the EKA179 LON module will have its **last-time-buy deadline in August 2026.** We encourage you to prepare your transition to the new AK-CC 25 Pro & Pro BT controllers. **Affected products** **Replacement guidance** All the controllers listed above can be replaced by the new AK-CC25 Pro (BT) with the limitation of support for LON communication. As LON communication has been declared obsolete by its technology provider, Danfoss will no longer integrate service support for this in our new products. For service replacements (spare parts), a limited number of AK-CC 210 controllers and accompanying EKA 179A LON option modules have been secured and will be made available for service replacement only. ## EKE 315 Superheat Controller now available The EKE 315 Superheat Controller is now available for industrial refrigeration applications. It is designed to support efficient installation, reliable operation, and straightforward commissioning across a wide range of superheat control applications. The EKE 315 offers efficient installation with quick setup, reduces downtime and labor costs. An intuitive wizard streamlines the commissioning process, making it user-friendly and straightforward. Simplified connections are achieved with a single 24 V AC or DC supply, ensuring seamless integration with expansion valves, such as the AKV, AKVA, or Danfoss motorized expansion valves (type ICM with ICAD) via a 4–20 mA signal exchange. Built for robust industrial use, the EKE 315 features precise control via a 4–20 mA analog input and output. Reliable communication is facilitated through Modbus RTU RS485, ensuring effective bus communication across your systems. It supports low‑GWP refrigerants, including ammonia, CO₂, hydrocarbons, and HFOs, ensuring long‑term compliance and reduced environmental impact. Multilingual support: 14 language options are available, enabling easier use and customization for a wide range of global users. Main advanced features - Modulating Thermostat (MTR) - Minimum Stable Superheat (MSS) - LoadApp for load-defined superheat - Suction Pressure Optimization (Po Optimization) for possible integration with System Manager SM-800A The [CoolConfig PC tool](https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/downloads/dcs/coolconfig/) supports project management by allowing settings to be replicated across multiple units and by simplifying documentation. This helps ensure consistency and ease of use when managing projects from one EKE 315 to several units. The EKE 315 can be used to service and replace the large installed base of EKC 315s units that were phased out years ago. **Sales codes** For more information, visit our [Danfoss Store](https://store.danfoss.com/p/080G5042) or contact your local sales representative. ## AK-CC55 Single Coil software version 2.30 now available New software version 2.30 is now available for AK-CC55 Single Coil (UI) case controllers. **Affected part numbers are 084B4082, 084B4083, 084B4182, and 084B4183.** This release corrects a bug in the defrost method using pulsing electrical heaters that was introduced in software version 2.24, and it also adds new functionality. The update is currently released as a web release and is available through the [AK-CC Connect app](https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/downloads/dcs/adap-kool-software/ak-cc/) or as an update file for [KoolProg](https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/downloads/dcs/koolprog/). From May 2026, this software update is also planned to be pre-installed on controllers leaving production. If the product is used as part of a production line, please update the setting files accordingly. **Details** Software version 2.30 provides a permanent correction for the issue identified in the defrost method using pulsing electrical heaters introduced in software version 2.24 (web release only). Version 2.30 also includes the following new functionality: - Fan ECO mode extended (always at night, at night cut-out, always at cut-out) - Fan ECO speed during defrost configurable - Leak alarm action with leak shutoff safety valve and alarm reset delay - Option to set ECO Fan and variable fan speed during leak alarm action **Affected products** - AK-CC55 Single Coil [084B4082](https://store.danfoss.com/p/084B4082) - AK-CC55 Single Coil [UI 084B4083](https://store.danfoss.com/p/084B4083) - AK-CC55 Single Coil [084B4182](https://store.danfoss.com/p/084B4182) - AK-CC55 Single Coil [UI 084B4183](https://store.danfoss.com/p/084B4183) For more information, please contact your local sales representative. ## AK-SM 800A Series software release 5.0, including SvW update Software release 5.0 is now available for the ADAP-KOOL™ System Manager 800A series. This release is accompanied by Danux package 4.14.017.194, which is recommended to be installed before loading the AK-SM800A application update. Both packages are available on [ADAP-KOOL support site](https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/downloads/dcs/adap-kool-software/ak-sm-800a/#tab-overview) **Software package 5.0 requires Danux 4.14.017.194** **Important notes on package 5.0 update** Please note that release R5.0.x includes important changes to the overall database structure. As a result, returning to an earlier software version after the update will not be supported. To ensure a smooth update process, we strongly recommend taking a full backup of the system database before starting the upgrade. As part of the update, existing History data will be automatically converted to the new format. The progress of this process can be followed under \[History Config --> Status\]. To help protect the data during conversion, we recommend avoiding unit resets while this process is running. The system can tolerate up to three resets during conversion; however, if a fourth reset occurs, any history data not yet converted will be lost. After the update, StoreView Web (SvW) embedded will become the default remote user interface. SvB5 will remain available for a limited period and is planned to be phased out in a future release. **Main release highlights** **Release 5.0.x is a major release for the SM800A series and is recommended for all customers.** Multiple updates and new features are included. Some of the main highlights are: - Default remote user interface now StoreView Web (SvW ’embedded’) - Increased capacity for EDF files (from 1500 to 3000) - Improved history function and memory management - Support for Alsmart Modbus/TCP - New caution prompts added when removing key application config (local screen only) - Improved SNMP performance - Security updates - Bug fixes **StoreView Web (embedded user interface - new)** The term SvW Embedded refers to the remote user interface (web screens) integrated directly into the System Manager. Following the update to R5.0.x, users can enter the IP address or URL of the System Manager into a standard web browser to access the interface. Instead of SvB5, the system will then open StoreView Web (SvW). SvW is the preferred remote user interface going forward and complements the already available SvW Cloud and SvW desktop solutions. - SvW comes in three variants o SvW ‘Cloud’ (requires internet connection) o SvW ‘Embedded’ – built into the System Manager (no internet required) o SvW Desktop – SvW for your PC (used to connect to http and https units) - SvW cloud can be accessed via [https://svw.danfoss.com](https://svw.danfoss.com) and can be used in conjunction with HTTPS enabled 800A units - To download SvWDesktop (supporting http/https 800A units) first log into the cloud version [https://svw.danfoss.com](https://svw.danfoss.com), then via the ‘More…’ tab, you can download the desktop version. **Updated History function** The *Histor*y function has been updated to improve system management of the data and to assign dedicated flash memory for new Active and Archive directories. **Improvements include**: - Strict boundary protection – memory allocation can no longer be overfilled - Dedicated assigned memory allocation for new Database Directories - New Active Database Directory for polled points (8GB) - New Archive Database Directory (2GB) - History is stored as monthly files within the Active directory until either capacity is reached or the start of a new month – then last file will be automatically transferred to the Archive directory – this ensures the Active directory cannot overspill / delete data / freeze system - History in Active directory can always be viewed via the History view screen - History migrating to Archive directory will be converted to CSV and zipped to minimize size and maximize the length of time it can be stored (2GB). Any transitioned monthly file in Archive can be downloaded - The maximum number of polled points is updated to 3000\* \*it may not be possible to log 3000 points at max frequency (1 min) on slow field bus (i.e. Serial Modbus) – in this case the sample rates can be increased - Conversion from current history architecture to the new format is done automatically and starts after the system has been updated to version 5.0.x software **Important changes** For security reasons, the service tool (ST-500) port is disabled by default. To enable a remote service tool tunnel connection, enable the port via the \[Configuration > Security screen\]. Disable the port again when the tunnel is no longer needed. To comply with Cyber Security requirements, new user accounts must have strong passwords (8 characters, including 1 uppercase, digit, and special character). **Release R5.0 Full Change Log** For release 5.x Change Log please visit ADAP-KOOL® Support site and SvW Release Notes under information / application information panel. **Security** To help keep your Danfoss products secured and protected, we emphasize implementing cyber security best practices to maximize your protection against malicious attacks. **Software installation** *Step1*: Install Danux 4.14.017.194.lpk - Using StoreView Browser 5 / StoreView Web select OS update and proceed with Danux upgrade - Allow a few minutes to pass with the new OS installed Important notes: This file size package is large and depending on your network speed may take 10+ minutes to complete. **Do not interrupt power during the OS update. For systems utilizing DHCP it is advised that this update is performed locally, as IP address change is possible after rebooting.** *Step 2*: Update System Manager firmware package 5.0.19.spk - Using StoreView Browser 5 / StoreView Web or local USB Flash drive, select OS update and proceed software upgrade. Do not interrupt power during the software update - After installation is complete, review for correct system operation **Approved products** The tables below show the approved AK-SM 800A portfolio versions suitable for software 5.0. **Timing and Stock** Package 5.0 is released for general update and is available via [ADAP-KOOL® support site](https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/downloads/dcs/adap-kool-software/#tab-overview). Stock units will not be recalled or updated. ## New software release version 1.35 for AK-CC25 Pro & Pro BT A new software version 1.35 is now available for AK-CC25 Pro and Pro BT. The new SW comes with new security features such as mandatory password configuration, while it also resolves a bug in the condenser monitoring function. The main new functionality includes: - Security Update: Access code protection The new software version introduces enhanced security features including mandatory access code setup at first startup, configurable access levels for function keys and brute force attack prevention. The values of the access codes are protected, and the values cannot be read out from any interface once they have been set, however if users forget the access code it can be overwritten via KoolProg or via SM800A. Please note the exception; for the AK-CC25 Pro without Bluetooth, the access code can be disabled. - Bug fix: Condenser monitoring function A bug has been reported in the condenser monitoring function, resulting in the compressor not being cut-out if the measured condenser temperature exceeds the condenser block limit. The bug is only present if no condenser fan is defined on one of the digital outputs. This bug has been fixed with SW version 1.35. Products with the new SW version 1.35 installed from factory will be identified as PV 02. All AK-CC 25 Pro and Pro BT with previous PV versions can be updated manually via KoolProg or CC Connect. When receiving the new version or when making the SW update through CC Connect or Koolprog, please be aware of the updated security feature and the mandatory access code setup at first startup. For more information on how to set up the access code upon first start-up, and overwrite in case of forgotten access code, please refer to: - [The updated user guide](https://assets.danfoss.com/documents/latest/569101/BC515532816014en-010103.pdf) - [The FAQ on Danfoss website](https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/fix-and-troubleshooting/cooling-installer-hub/electronic-controllers-services-faqs/case-controller-faq/) - Or contact your local product support. ## New StoreView Web (SvW) release 3.4.2 We would like to inform you that SvW R3.4.2 has been released with a performance improvement for Store Maps. This hotfix improves the communication handling between SvW and AK-SM8xxA/AK-SM8xx, resulting in better Store Maps performance and a more stable user experience. **Timing and availability** Storeview Web (3.4.2) was released by Danfoss on March 2026 but may take up to 24 hours to take effect depending on browser versions. Storeview Web (3.4.2) is available via browser (svw.danfoss.com) and via desktop app, available from same location. Please note that Storeview Web requires connectivity to your System Manager. **Affected products** StoreView Web supports: - **AK-SM 800 series** (Recommended VG08.095 and above) - **AK-SM 800A series** (Recommended R3.0.12 spk and above) ## New software release version 2.31 for AK-CC55 Compact A new SW release is available for AK-CC55 Compact case controllers (v 2.31); 084B4081 & 084B4181. This brings a set of new and improved features (see below), while keeping the core application functionality of the controller unchanged. Currently, the update will only be released as a web-release, available via AK-CC Connect app or as update file for KoolProg. From May 2026 this SW update is also planned to come preinstalled on the controllers coming out of production, therefore if you are using the product as part of production line, please update the setting files accordingly. **New features** - Improved injection algorithm (improved SH control, flooding protection) - New refrigerants (R454A, R454C, R455A, R516A, R469A) - Support for stepper valve driver via 0-10V signal in applications with EEV valve (5-9) - Local Day/night schedule - Pulsing electrical defrost - Support 2 defrost stop sensors Variable speed compressor in applications with TXV valve (1-4) - Compressor safety monitoring via DI input - Fully flexible IO configuration in application 4 and 9 - New default settings for dewpoint-based rail-heat control - Prepared for KoolProg connection via Modbus RS-485 and KoolKey 2.1 (will be supported by future release of KoolProg – follow the dedicated PN) - Added performance indicators (visible in AK-CC Connect app – Performance dashboard) o Door opening history o Average defrost time o Number of high temp. alarms - Added temperature quality indicator ## New Superheat Controller Kit EKE 100 1VK We are excited to announce the launch of our new superheat controller kit EKE 100 1VK, designed to bring convenience and efficiency to your cold room applications. This innovative solution simplifies the ordering and stocking processes, improves installation ease, and ensures fast and reliable performance. **The superheat controller kit includes the following components:** 1. EKE 100 1V Superheat controller & valve driver with integrated display 2. DST P110 Pressure transmitter and cable 3. AKS 11 Temperature sensor 4. Bipolar coil for ETS 5M Customers can also purchase an ETS 5M valve to complement the kit, depending on capacity needs. This comprehensive package is ideal for applications in air conditioning, commercial refrigeration, and food retail, providing precise superheat control and effectively regulating superheat to the lowest possible level in a short timeframe. **Benefits** - Simplified ordering and stocking - Ease of installation with no missing parts - Fast and reliable performance - Energy consumption reduction, even amidst load variations **Ordering & availability** The superheat controller kit is now available for sales. Code number for ordering: SH Controller Kit EKE 100 1VK: [080G9100](https://store.danfoss.com/en/Climate-Solutions-for-cooling/Electronic-controls/Controllers-and-drivers-for-stepper-motor-valves/EKE-100-1VK/SH-Controller-kit%2C-EKE-100-1VK/p/080G9100) **More information** For detailed product information: ## New service cable for EKE 100/110 products We are pleased to inform you about an important update regarding the service cable of EKE 100 and EKE 110 controllers. To ensure compatibility with the latest KoolKey version PV04, we are introducing a new service cable. Product details Current cable 080G5058 New cable 080G5067 The existing service cable (080G5058) will be phased out and replaced by the new service cable (080G5067). This change is necessary to maintain seamless communication between EKE 100/110 and KoolProg using KoolKey PV04. **Compability** Note: All new orders for KoolKey will be delivered with PV04 versions. **Affected controllers** - 080G5050 - Superheat controller and valve driver EKE 100 1V IP00 - 080G5051 - Superheat controller and valve driver EKE 100 1V IP20 - 080G5052 - Superheat controller and valve driver EKE 100 1V IP20 with display - 080G5055 - Superheat controller and valve driver EKE 100 2V IP00 - 080G5056 - Superheat controller and valve driver EKE 100 2V IP20 - 080G5057 - Superheat controller and valve driver EKE 100 2V IP20 with display - 080G5066 - Superheat controller and valve driver EKE 100 2V IP20 - 080G5059 - Injection controller EKE 110 1V IP20 **Availability & ordering** For all future orders, please ensure that you order the new service cable (080G5067) instead of the previous cable (080G5058). This will guarantee compatibility and functionality when used with EKE 100/110 controllers, KoolKey, and the KoolProg PC tool. The new service cable will be available for sale starting from week 5 of 2026. ## Market release of AK-CC25 Pro BT case controller **Bluetooth-enabled AK-CC25 Pro BT** – expansion of the new ADAP-KOOL® CC-25 case controller family **AK-CC25 Pro highlights** New modern design and improved user experience - White LED display and backlit capacitive touch buttons to only show the relevant UI elements - Built-in BLE for connectivity with AK-CC Connect mobile app for fast and easy service & commissioning (AK-CC25 Pro BT only) - New and improved functions in the mobile app: FW update, performance dashboards, Wizard for guided field installation and commissioning (AK-CC25 Pro BT only) Best-in class application coverage in a single variant - Support for variable speed compressors, dual circuits, dual compressor - Full parameter MT/LT switch for optimized performance - Fully flexible I/O configuration for customized applications Food safety & energy efficiency - Robust design for reliable operation with minimum downtime - VSC enables MTR for optimal temperature in a display cabinet Improved connectivity and monitoring - Modbus RS-485 built-in - Modbus over Wi-Fi via external gateway - BLE built-in (AK-CC25 Pro BT only) **Availability & ordering** The initial is limited to countries/customers in Europe and Turkey, as we are still working on production capacity ramp-up and regional compliance approvals (e.g. UL). The product store will reflect this. **EKC/AK-CC 2xx Phase out** With the launch of AK-CC25, the phase out process of the existing EKC 202 and AK-CC 2xx controllers has been initiated. Please discuss with your Danfoss sales contact about the transition plan and forecast. ## Release of AK-CC25 Pro case controllers to market We are pleased to announce the market release of the new family member of ADAP-KOOL® case controllers – AK-CC25 Pro, an advanced controller for plug-in and remote TXV cases. **AK-CC25 Pro highlights** **New modern design and improved user experience:** - White LED display and backlit capacitive touch buttons to only show the relevant UI elements - Built-in BLE for connectivity with AK-CC Connect mobile app for fast and easy service & commissioning (AK-CC25 Pro BT only) - New and improved functions in the mobile app: FW update, performance dashboards, Wizard for guided field installation and commissioning (AK-CC25 Pro BT only) **Best-in class application coverage in a single variant:** - Support for variable speed compressors, dual circuits, dual compressor - Full parameter MT/LT switch for optimized performance - Fully flexible I/O configuration for customized applications **Food safety & energy efficiency:** - Robust design for reliable operation with minimum downtime - VSC enables MTR for optimal temperature in a display cabinet **Improved connectivity and monitoring:** - Modbus RS-485 built-in - Modbus over Wi-Fi via external gateway - BLE built-in (AK-CC25 Pro BT only) **Availability & Ordering** The initial is limited to countries/customers in Europe and Turkey, as we are still working on production capacity ramp-up and regional compliance approvals (e.g. UL). The product store will reflect this. **EKC/AK-CC 2xx phase out** With the launch of AK-CC25, the phase out process of the existing EKC 202 and AK-CC 2xx controllers has been initiated. Please discuss with your Danfoss sales contact about the transition plan and forecast. ### 2025 ## New AK-SM 800A Danux available (4.14.017.194) We have received reports describing issues related to the creation and deletion of users in the AK-SM 800A System Manager. To address this, a new Operating System (Danux) file has been released — version 4.14.017.194. A bug was identified in a Linux library responsible for user management. This issue caused the generation of lock files preventing normal user operations such as adding or deleting users. The fix implemented in Danux v4.14.017.194 automatically removes these lock files, thereby restoring full user management functionality. If your System Manager shows symptoms of being unable to add or remove users, please install the updated operating system Danux v4.14.017.194 following the best practices below. **Software installation** Perform a unit backup and check for any open alarms before proceeding with update. Install Danux 4.14.017.194.lpk) - Using StoreView Browser 5 / StoreView Web select OS update and proceed with Danux upgrade - Allow a few minutes to pass with the new OS installed **Important notes** This file size package is large and depending on your network speed may take 10+ minutes to complete. Do not interrupt power during the OS update. For systems utilizing DHCP it is advised that this update is performed locally, as IP address change is possible after re-booting. Software can be found on Danfoss homepage: ## AK-SM 800A series, software release 4.3.1 including security updates Danfoss announces a new software release of the ADAP-KOOL™ System Manager 800A series. Please note, a new Danux package (4.14.016.194) accompanies this release and it is recommended to be installed prior to loading the AK-SM800A application update. Both packages can be found on [ADAP-KOOL support site.](https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/downloads/dcs/adap-kool-software/ak-sm-800a/#tab-overview) **Software package 4.3.1 requires Danux 4.14.016.194.** **Software release 4.3.1 security certifiction** As part of our ongoing commitment to product security and regulatory compliance, we are pleased to inform you that AK-SM800A software version 4.3.1 complies with the latest cybersecurity requirements under the Radio Equipment Directive (RED) 2014/53/EU, including the upcoming provisions outlined in Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/30, efective from August 1, 2025. These new EU requirements apply to all radio equipment with internet connectivity and/or the ability to process personal data, and include safeguards to: - Prevent unauthorized access and data breaches - Protect against misuse of networks and services To support compliance with these enhanced regulations, our development processes follow **cybersecurity-by-design principles** and are certified according to **IEC 62443-4-1**, the internationally recognized standard for secure product development. This certifiction demonstrates our structured approach to managing cybersecurity risks throughout the entire product lifecycle. Our goal is to ensure that our customers benefit fom solutions that are not only compliant with EU regulations but also aligned with global cybersecurity best practices reinforcing trust and reliability in connected environments. **Important Changes** - One key change is that the [Service Tool (ST-500)](https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/downloads/dcs/adap-kool-software/ak-st-500/) port is now disabled by default. This helps reduce potential exter nal access risks. If remote access via the Service Tool is needed, the port can be temporarily enabled through the security settings, and we strongly recommend disabling it again after use. - Additionally, to further strengthen system protection, all new user accounts are now required to follow stronger password rules, including minimum character length and complexity. Existing user accounts are not afected unless they are required to change their password. These updates are in line with the industry’s best practices and regulatory expectations, and they support our commitment to delivering secure and reliable system solutions for our customers. **Software Release 4.3.1 main highlights** Security: - Cryptographic validation of AK-SM800A package - Hardened UPK update against file injetion - Permanent disabling of SSH connection - Post-authenticated external control of system web interface configuation settings - Sanitization of input fields - potect from code injection - System now requires user to change password immediately after first loin - Update (block) access to serial console for the root user - Prevent user corruption of webserver-configuation - Update nginx and mail to support TLS version 1.2 - Block sweet32 cipher suite (Nginx) - Add user message under all HTTP/S configuation areas - New user accounts require strong passwords New features: - Add new A2L Refrigerants for 800A Rack Control - Add 90-day password/account expiry - MCX Lighting control - Customer request import Analog Input Bug fixes: - Resetting Issue found when a 800A converted database from 800 that had Alarm Logger - Session manager does not allow to create a new password when the old expires - NTP timing issue **Software Installation** Perform a unit backup and check for any open alarms before proceeding with update. R4.3.1 requires Danux 4.14.016.194 to be installed firs, followed by the 4.3.1 fimware package. After installation of Danux and 4.3.1 packages be sure to perform a ‘soft reset’ via the ‘Config -> omm screen’ and use the ‘Press to reset’ this unit button. **Step1 (install Danux 4.14.016.194.lpk)** - Using StoreView Browser 5 / StoreView Web select OS update and proceed with Danux upgrade - Important notes: This file sie package is large and depending on your network speed may take 10+ minutes to complete. Do not interrupt power during the OS update. For systems utilizing DHCP it is advised that this update is per- formed locally, as IP address change is possible after re-booting. **Step 2 (update System Manager fimware (package 4.3.1 spk))** - Using StoreView Browser 5 / StoreView Web or local USB Flash drive, select OS update and proceed software upgrade. Do not interrupt power during the software update. **Step 3 (perform soft reset to fully apply packages)** - After installation of Danux and 4.3.1 packages be sure to perform a ‘soft reset’ via the ‘Config -> omm screen’ and use the ‘press to reset this unit’ button. **Step 4 (review)** - After installation is complete, review for correct system operation. **Approved products** The table below shows approved AK-SM 800A portfolio versions suitable for software 4.3.1 **Timing and stock** Package 4.3.1 is released for general update and is available via ADAP-KOOL® [support site](https://www.danfoss.com/en/service-and-support/downloads/dcs/adap-kool-software/ak-sm-800a/#tab-downloads). Stock units will not be recalled or updated. **Security** To help keep your Danfoss products secure and protected, we emphasize implementing cyber security at best practices to maximize your protection against malicious attacks. ## StoreView Web (SvW) release 3.4.1 Danfoss is pleased to announce that a new version of Storeview Web (SvW) is available, version 3.4.1. The main highlights of this release include improvements for usability, configuation and interface and various bug fies. **Timing and availability** Storeview Web (3.4.1) is released from Danfoss in June 2025 but may take up to 24 hours to take efect depending on browser versions. Storeview Web (3.4.1) is available via browser (svw.danfoss.com) and via desktop app, available from same location. Please note that Storeview Web requires connectivity to your System Manager. Special Notes Support for the End Of Life (EoL) AK-SM800 Configuation wizards in SvW has been blocked due to unpredictable results. Addressing this issue would require modifiction to the AK-SM800, which is no longer available for service. **Afected products** StoreView Web supports: AK-SM 800 series (Recommended VG08.095 and above) AK-SM 800A series (Recommended R3.0.12 spk and above) More information and news about the current and future updates can be found on Danfoss.com. **Storeview Web 3.4.1- Change Log** ## Release of the redesigned Danfoss Gas Sensor product family We are pleased to announce the release of the newly redesigned DGS (Danfoss Gas Sensor) product family. The redesigned devices maintain the same core functionalities as the previous generation while introducing several enhanced features. The updated products will be launched under new product codes **Key changes in the redesign** This redesign does not affect the main functions of the device. The improvements include: - Isolated Modbus circuit - Modbus connector that now includes GND and is separated from the power supply - Improved EMC immunity - Case predrilled for cable passage, with metallic plugs to maintain the IP rating - 45-degree connectors for easier access **The images below illustrate the changes in the redesigned DGS device** **Compatibility and Accessories** Other products and accessories in the DGS portfolio (including spare sensors, the handheld service tool, strobe & horn, and power supply) remain unchanged and are fully compatible with the redesigned DGS product family. The redesigned DGS version will be compatible only with the AK SM 800A. **Availability and Additional Information** The redesigned products will be available from September 2025. A stock of current DGS products, compatible with previous versions of the System Manager prior to the AK-SM 800A, will still be available for gas sensor replacements. If you need additional information, please contact your local Danfoss sales representative.
